page RecipeServeWithNginx(path: "/recipes/serve-with-nginx", title: "Serve a site with nginx — Recipes", description: "1.") {
    RecipeShell("Serve a site with nginx", summary: "1. Add a `server` block. Pick the `try_files` line for your kind of build:     ```nginx server \{ listen 443 ssl http2; server_name example.com; root /var/www/site;         gzip_static on;                          # serve the .gz files the build wrote         location / \{ try_files $uri $uri/ $uri.html =404; # a static build # try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;  # a single-page build \} error_page 404 /404.html;         location = /sw.js \{ add_header Cache-Control \"no-cache\"; \} location ~* \\.(webp|avif|jpg|jpeg|png)$ \{ add_header Cache-Control \"public, max-age=31536000, immutable\"; \}         add_header X-Content-Type-Options nosniff always; add_header Referrer-Policy strict-origin-when-cross-origin always; add_header X-Frame-Options DENY always; # add_header Content-Security-Policy \"…as in build/_headers…\" always; \} ```  2. Upload the build with any tool. For example:     ```bash rsync -a --delete build/ server:/var/www/site/ ```  3. Reload nginx.  **Verify it:** `curl -I` a page and check the headers. Ask for a compressed copy and check that nginx sends the build's `.gz` file:  ```bash curl -sI -H \"Accept-Encoding: gzip\" https://example.com/app.js ```  The response has `Content-Encoding: gzip`.", outputs: [], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Build a Docker image", to: "/recipes/docker-image"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Check a deploy", to: "/recipes/check-a-deploy"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Deploy to Cloudflare Pages", to: "/recipes/deploy-to-cloudflare-pages")], source: "md-docs/recipes/serve-with-nginx.md", how: false, hasVariations: false) {
    }
}
